            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Final setup (correct form): $X(s)=\\int_{0^-}^{\\infty} u(t)e^{-st}\\,dt$. A common confusion is using bilateral bounds, omitting $0^-$, or writing only $e^{-t}$ without the full $e^{-st}$ weight.",
